  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q83-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "34",
    "prompt": "Use the identity $a^3-b^3=(a-b)(a^2+ab+b^2)$ to rationalise the denominator of",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q83-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac1{1+\\sqrt[3]2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4}{3}$.\n\nApply the identity with $a=1$ and $b=-\\sqrt[3]2$.",
          "worked": "Let $t=\\sqrt[3]2$. The supplied identity with $a=1$, $b=-t$ gives $(1+t)(1-t+t^2)=1+t^3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{1+\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4}{(1+\\sqrt[3]2)(1-\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4)}\\\\\\frac1{1+\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4}{1+2}\\\\\\frac1{1+\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q84-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac1{\\sqrt2-\\sqrt[3]2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{(2+\\sqrt2\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4)(\\sqrt2+1)}2$.\n\nUse the cubic identity, then rationalise $2(\\sqrt2-1)$.",
          "worked": "The supplied identity uses $a=\\sqrt2$ and $b=\\sqrt[3]2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{\\sqrt2-\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{2+\\sqrt2\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4}{(\\sqrt2)^3-(\\sqrt[3]2)^3}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt2-\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{2+\\sqrt2\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4}{2(\\sqrt2-1)}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt2-\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{(2+\\sqrt2\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4)(\\sqrt2+1)}{2(\\sqrt2-1)(\\sqrt2+1)}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt2-\\sqrt[3]2}&=\\frac{(2+\\sqrt2\\sqrt[3]2+\\sqrt[3]4)(\\sqrt2+1)}2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      }
    ]
